            "block_content": "19.19 Part-time employees hired on or after June 23, 2002, and before September 24, 2006 who are not assigned a full-time schedule, but work in excess of thirty (30) regular hours in a work week, shall receive time and one half (1 $ \\frac{1}{2} $) for those hours worked over thirty (30) hours up and including thirty five (35). Any part-time employee working in excess of thirty-five (35) regular hours then all hours worked will be paid at the minimum full time rate per hour or their current rate whichever is greater.",
